<title>USA: California retail diesel fell in week ended May 14.</title>
<headline>California retail diesel fell in week ended May 14.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The price of diesel fuel at California gas stations fell five cents a gallon as of May 14, weakened by declining wholesale markets, according to a weekly report from the California Energy Commission (CEC).</p>
<p>For the week ended May 14, diesel fuel prices were highest at southern California stations, averaging $1.359 cents a gallon.</p>
<p>Northern California diesel fuel averaged $1.357 cents, while stations in central California averaged 1.277 cents, the CEC said.</p>
<p>((David Brinkerhoff, Los Angeles bureau +1 213 380 2014))</p>
